abstract: "Temperature, conductivity, dissolved oxygen, fluorescence, photosynthetic\
  \ active radiation, turbidity, and coloured dissolved organic matter data collected\
  \ from 2012 to present by the Hakai Institute in waters surrounding Calvert Island,\
  \ Johnstone Strait, and Quadra Island areas.\n\nThis includes datasets made by oceanographic\
  \ profiler instruments (RBR XR-620, RBR Concerto, RBR Maestro, and Seabird SBE 19plus\
  \ v2) which have been automatically processed by following respective manufacturer's\
  \ guidelines (see Hakai Water Properties Profile Processing and QA/QC Procedure\
  \ Manual). This also includes a dataset from a C-PROOF (Canadian Pacific Robotic\
  \ Ocean Observing Facility) Wirewalker, a wave-powered profiler moored in Bute Inlet,\
  \ a fjord on the British Columbia coast.\n\nThe provisional processed CTD data are\
  \ then quality controlled by applying a series of tests that are following the QARTOD\
  \ standards and more tests specific to the Hakai Institute data (see Hakai Water\
  \ Properties Profile Processing and QA/QC Procedure Manual). The research CTD dataset\
  \ provides a subset of the provisional dataset which has been manually reviewed\
  \ and judged good for science quality level.\n\nTwo versions of the Wirewalker record\
  \ are included: provisional data offloaded directly from the instrument, which is\
  \ the more complete, and real-time data received via satellite, which is the more\
  \ current. \n\n\n\nData were collected by the Hakai Institute Oceanography Program,\
  \ the Nearshore Program, and the Juvenile Salmon Program."
